+/** Product-wide output contract, injected into every DeepViewer conversation. */
+export const FILE_DELIVERY_PROMPT = `File delivery is required in DeepViewer. Whenever the user asks you to generate or export an image, video, audio, document, archive, or any other file, deliver every final output as an attachment card before ending your response.
+Use the present tool with the existing file paths and concise descriptions. This applies to files created through image_generate, Bash, code execution, MCP, and other plugins. Tool output, inline images, Markdown links, path text, and a statement that a file was generated do not replace attachment delivery.
+The final delivered file must be inside the current workspace. DeepViewer normalizes generated outputs and present calls into the workspace outputs directory. Use the workspace paths returned by those tools. Never present the internal attachments/v1/objects path: that is a read-only model cache, not the original user delivery.
+Preserve existing filenames and formats. For other tools that return an external or temporary source file, call present on that source: DeepViewer will publish a correctly named workspace file and return its canonical path. Do not manually copy, rename, or convert an already delivered output unless the user asks. If delivery fails, use the existing original file to retry; do not spend another generation call to fix a delivery problem.
+Only present real, successfully generated final outputs; do not present input/reference files or internal scratch files. Never claim a missing or failed file was delivered. If saving or presenting fails, fix the failure when possible or explain the unresolved issue in the final response.`
