@@ -0,0 +1,123 @@
+---
+description: "Token-gated static route that lends a workspace HTML entry a real HTTP origin, so the right-Sidebar browser can frame a page together with its own relative assets."
+kind: "package-reference"
+---
+
+# @deepseek-ai/dsh-host-preview-static
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+Lend one workspace HTML entry a real HTTP origin for the right Sidebar's browser tab. The browser tab cannot frame `dsh-resource://file/**`, and a blob URL would cut a page off from its own relative stylesheets, scripts, and images — so this plugin serves the entry and its sibling files over `/deepviewer-preview-static/<token>/…` instead.
+
+A capability is minted per previewed entry through the `site` RPC on `/deepviewer-preview` and pins the entry's own directory: every asset request is resolved inside that directory after both a lexical and a `realpath` containment check, so neither a crafted path nor a symlink can walk out of the workspace. Tokens are opaque, unguessable, expiring, and bounded in number, so the route is never a general file server. Names that must never reach a browser — `.git`, `node_modules`, `.env*`, and private-key material — are refused outright. The route is mounted only on a loopback bind.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Use this package](#use-this-package)
+- [Understand the implementation](#understand-the-implementation)
+- [Model Experience](#model-experience)
+- [Known Limitations and Deferred Work](#known-limitations-and-deferred-work)
+
+-----
+
+<a id="use-this-package"></a>
+## Use this package
+
+Compose this plugin in the Web host, beside the browser tab that consumes it. It registers itself and needs no configuration.
+
+### Minimal configuration
+
+```yaml
+- name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-host-preview-static'
+```
+
+The browser half mints a capability by calling the `site` endpoint with `{ absolutePath }` — the entry's **absolute** path — and receives `{ url, expiresAt, entryPath }`, where `entryPath` is that path relative to the workspace this plugin resolved. It frames the returned relative URL and shows `entryPath` in its address bar.
+
+### Who decides which workspace owns the file
+
+This plugin, and nobody else. The caller cannot name a workspace reliably: a `dsh-resource://file/session/…` address carries a path relative to the *Session's* cwd whenever the file sits under it (see `fileAddressFor` in `@deepseek-ai/dsh-util-workspace-path`), and a Session's cwd may be a subdirectory that equals no registered workspace root. So the caller rebuilds the absolute path from the Session cwd it holds, and this plugin picks the **tightest** registered root that contains it:
+
+- a file under several nested workspaces resolves to the longest matching root;
+- a root must match on a path boundary, so `/work` never claims `/workbench`;
+- a file no workspace contains is refused with `outside-workspace` rather than served, which is the fence that keeps this route from becoming a general file server.
+
+Workspace membership by `sessionIds` is deliberately not consulted: that account is validated against a Session's cwd, so it excludes exactly the nested-cwd case above.
+
+### RPC failures
+
+| Code | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| `bad-request` | The payload was not `{ absolutePath: string }`, or the endpoint is unknown |
+| `outside-workspace` | No registered workspace contains the file |
+| `not-loopback` | The server is not bound to loopback, so the route is not mounted |
+| `internal` | The entry is blocked, missing, not HTML, or otherwise refused by the containment fence |
+
+### What the route enforces
+
+| Condition | Answer |
+|---|---|
+| Unknown, expired, or evicted token | 404 |
+| Server-side route but no capability segment | 404 |
+| Asset resolves outside the capability root | 404 |
+| Symlink whose `realpath` leaves the capability root | 404 |
+| Blocked name (`.git`, `node_modules`, `.env*`, `*.pem`, …) | 404 |
+| Asset larger than 16 MiB | 404 |
+| Any method other than GET/HEAD | 405 |
+| Request path with no extension | the entry, so a client-side route can deep-link |
+
+A miss and a containment rejection answer identically on purpose: the route never describes the filesystem.
+
+Served HTML is appended with a small navigation bridge that reports the frame's location to its parent and accepts `back`/`forward`/`reload` commands, so the address bar can follow in-page navigation without the framed document gaining a same-origin identity. Responses also carry `frame-ancestors 'self'` and `connect-src 'none'`.
+
+-----
+
+<a id="understand-the-implementation"></a>
+## Understand the implementation
+
+<details>
+<summary>Implementation internals — click to expand</summary>
+
+### Design concept
+
+The plugin is two seats over one capability table. `apply` constructs a `PreviewCapabilities` and registers:
+
+1. the `site` RPC on `/deepviewer-preview` — resolves the containing workspace with `containingWorkspace()` over `ctx.workspaceRegistry.list()`, mints a capability rooted at the entry's directory, and answers the URL plus the workspace-relative entry path;
+2. the `/deepviewer-preview-static` prefix route — splits the token from the asset path, looks the capability up, and serves the asset.
+
+Both registrations are effect-scoped, so disposing the fiber releases them.
+
+### Why the route skips Connection's browser authentication
+
+The framed document runs in an opaque origin, so it carries no browser-session cookie and could never satisfy `ctx.connection.requestRejection`. Access control is therefore the capability token itself: 24 random bytes, a 30-minute lifetime, at most 32 live at once. That is also why the plugin withholds the route entirely on an all-interfaces bind — on a LAN bind the token would be the only thing standing between a peer and the user's workspace, and the RPC reports that state instead of serving.
+
+### Source map
+
+| File | Role |
+|---|---|
+| [`src/index.ts`](src/index.ts) | `apply`: the capability RPC and the token-gated prefix route |
+| [`src/capability.ts`](src/capability.ts) | Capability table, containment fence, MIME table, security headers, navigation bridge |
+
+</details>
+
+-----
+
+## Model Experience
+
+None, as the route answers browser asset requests and registers nothing model-facing.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+None; this package neither assembles nor sends a provider request.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+These limits define when a previewed page is not yet covered. They are current package constraints, not a task backlog.
+
+- **`connect-src 'none'` blocks page-side fetches** — a previewed page cannot call a local API through `fetch` or `XMLHttpRequest`. Relaxing this needs its own review, because the framed document would then reach the host's own routes.
+- **A capability is rooted at one directory** — assets above the entry's directory (`../shared/style.css`) are refused, since containment is anchored at the entry. A page laid out across sibling directories is not yet covered.
+- **The route refuses key material** — `.pem`, `.key`, `.crt` and friends answer 404 even when a page legitimately needs them.
+- **No live reload** — a change to the entry re-mints only on reload; nothing watches the workspace.
+
+**Runtime invariant:** No companion is published. The RPC channel and the prefix route live exactly as long as this plugin; the capability table is instance state owned by `apply`, and every capability dies with it.
